@209 = ~preacher of flames~
@21 = ~Preacher of Flames~
@22 = ~PREACHER OF FLAMES: Fire has long inspired admiration among humanoids. Pyromaniacs kindle it for the sheer pleasure of watching it consume everything. Wizards value its destructive power. Tacticians use it to frighten, repel and corner their enemies.
Some clerics also become fascinated by this force of nature, and the less prudent may even deem it worthy of worship. By rejecting their original deity, they lose their ability to cast divine spells. Among these fallen priests, those most fanatically devoted to fire and destruction sometimes attract the attention of dark powers, usually demonic in origin. These powers restore their spellcasting, but corrupt it with fire and strip it of all restorative abilities. They turn the fallen clerics into instruments of devastation, without necessarily revealing their intentions.

Advantages:
- Gains additional fire spells:
     Level 1: Flame Dart, Scorcher, Burning Hands.
     Level 2: Magma Bomb, Explosion, Rain of Fire, Lower Fire Resistance, Fire Seeds.
     Level 3: Blazing Weapon, Fire Shield (Red), Fireball, Flame Arrow, Melf's Minute Meteors.
     Level 4: Conjure Lesser Fire Elemental, Ignition, Fire Form, Lower Fire Resistance II, Fire Breath.
     Level 5: Call Fire Servant, Ardent Mantle, Fire Mark, Mass Protection from Fire, Pulverization.
     Level 6: Heat Aura, Elemental Fireball, Conjure Fire Elemental, Detonation, Exploding Mephits.
     Level 7: Incineration, Fire Trap.
- Gains 10% fire resistance at level 1, plus 3% per subsequent level.
- May use Burning Palm once per day at level 10, gaining another daily use every 3 levels thereafter.
- May charm a fire elemental once per day at level 13, gaining another daily use at level 20.

Disadvantages:
- Cannot cast ANY healing, curing or restoration spells.
- Cannot turn undead.
- Must be true neutral or neutral evil.
- Cannot dual-class: his obsession with fire rules out any other career.
- Does not receive a divine symbol at level 25, having severed all ties to the gods.

BURNING PALM:
After activating this ability, the preacher has two rounds to touch an opponent. A successful touch deals 1d6 points of fire damage per two preacher levels. If he fails to hit within that time, the spell is lost.

CHARM FIRE ELEMENTAL:
The preacher can attempt to control any fire elemental by touching it. The target may save with a -1 penalty per 5 preacher levels to resist. If it fails, it serves the preacher for 5 turns.~

@203 = ~Burning Palm~
@204 = ~Burning Palm:

Grants one additional daily use of Burning Palm.~
@205 = ~Charm Fire Elemental~

// Texts not included in BGEE
